VALUES ('2026-W31', NULL, 'S2 "Hold with hawkish framing; capex mixed; the box holds" (40%)', 'Partial', '[{"grade":"Partial","id":"S1","probability":30,"source":"Scorecard Ledger"},{"grade":"Partial","id":"S3","probability":30,"source":"Scorecard Ledger"}]'::jsonb, 'valid - Phase 3 held; index +1.05% while breadth ran 71.76 → 66.60 inside the week, leadership compressed to two names, credit widened a 2nd week', 'valid but weakening - Phase 5 held a 4th week on level, but BTC fell 3.9% into the most risk-on tape in months and the 3-week ETF streak broke to outflow', 'Bounded oil in an $85-100 band across all three branches and Brent went through the floor to $83.30 on a negotiated Hormuz reopening - two-sided is not the same as wide enough. For the 2nd straight week a correctly-named trigger produced the opposite tape: the market priced AI capex as a relative trade (MSFT +16% vs META −10% in 24h), which a directional-only scenario table cannot express. And no branch allowed for vol to compress - VIX printed 15.99 against S2''s 17-21 and S3''s >22. Also carried zero Korea exposure into the KOSPI''s worst month on record (China DUV breakthrough), the 2nd dateless structural shock in four weeks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, NULL)
