VALUES ('2026-W36', '0397be83-59f0-5122-933f-1e38f4edf305', 'S1 "Hawkish resilience, exceptional AI holds the index" (45%)', 'Partial', '[{"grade":"Not","id":"S2","note":"The soft half of the trigger fired on JOLTS and ISM employment, but 162K payrolls killed the 0K–100K condition and every target failed: breadth fell to 64.01%, the Russell never approached 3,020, and the 2Y rose instead of falling.","probability":30,"source":"sidecar 2026-W37","targets_hit":0,"targets_n":6,"title":"Labor cools enough to broaden without breaking"},{"grade":"Partial","id":"S3","note":"The hot-tail Brent trigger above $95 fired exactly as written for the fifth week running, and again nothing transmitted: VIX 14.53, HY 265 bps, no equity band broken.","probability":25,"source":"sidecar 2026-W37","targets_hit":0,"targets_n":7,"title":"Either labor tail breaks the soft landing"}]'::jsonb, 'valid - Phase 3 held and internals weakened: breadth 68.8 → 64.0, CNN F&G into Fear at 42, Broadcom and Lululemon punished while the index sat flat and credit tightened', 'valid - Phase 1 held; third straight weekly ETF inflow, OI rebuilt +7%, the NFP dip to $79.2K was bought, but no impulse and ETH fund demand collapsed 74%', 'Bounded Brent below $92 for the third time in five weeks and it settled $96 on a US-Iran escalation ladder; coupled Broadcom''s multi-year AI outlook to a positive price reaction when the tape punished a marginal guide miss; assumed SOL-led crypto while flows rotated BTC-only; and the oil trigger fired for the fifth week without a confirming risk regime, so the oil leg needs its own scenario axis.', 6, 9, 0.155, false, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-09T00:00:00Z')
