VALUES ('2026-W37', 'e11478b0-6904-5980-aaf7-0f968ac1730b', 'S2 "Hot-enough CPI keeps the hike live while oil taxes the tape" (40%)', 'Materialized', '[{"grade":"Not","id":"S1","note":"Core CPI printed 0.3% and every leg inverted; only HY closed on the edge of its band at 270 bps.","probability":35,"source":"sidecar 2026-W38","targets_hit":1,"targets_n":10,"title":"Cool CPI kills the hike and breadth gets its repair window"},{"grade":"Not","id":"S3","note":"Iran''s 10-ship strike wave and the Saudi output collapse fired the oil half, but the trigger was a conjunction and no confirming leg printed: VIX 15.84, HY 270 bps, breadth 54.67% at its worst.","probability":25,"source":"sidecar 2026-W38","targets_hit":0,"targets_n":8,"title":"The chokepoint converts and brings a risk regime with it"}]'::jsonb, 'valid - Phase 3 held while breadth broke 60% (64.0 → 56.5, 54.7 intraweek), CNN F&G fell to 33 and an Oracle beat faded, with the index only −0.8% and HY +5 bps', 'valid but weakening - Phase 1 held above the $74K falsifier, but BTC ETFs flipped to four outflow sessions (−$463M), $80K failed, and sponsorship rotated to ETH', 'The base case''s mechanism landed almost exactly (core CPI 0.3%, Brent $95–$108, hike odds to ~86%) and was still priced at only 40%, so Brier punished under-confidence, not direction. The two missed bands were both composition: breadth fell through the 58% floor while the index held, and ETH broke to a January high on its own ETF inflow while BTC bled, repeating R10 by treating a BTC-only flow streak as the regime.', 9, 11, 0.545, false, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-14T00:00:00Z')
