VALUES ('2026-W38', '829138cc-3d63-5d77-b63a-904c581e88ab', 'S1 "The Fed hikes with a path while oil stays above $100" (45%)', 'Partial', '[{"grade":"Partial","id":"S2","note":"Not one trigger clause fired, yet the four bands S1 missed — VIX 13–16, BTC $79K–$85K, ETH $2,550–$2,850, gold $4,380–$4,600 — all landed here, plus HY at the top of its range.","probability":30,"source":"sidecar 2026-W39","targets_hit":5,"targets_n":11,"title":"Hike and done: the Fed buys credibility and the tape exhales"},{"grade":"Not","id":"S3","note":"The 20Y tailed 2 bp at a record 5.42% and the 10Y touched 5.04%, but the trigger was written as a conjunction requiring the 30Y above 5.60%, which never came, and no VIX, HY or breadth leg confirmed for a sixth straight week.","probability":25,"source":"sidecar 2026-W39","targets_hit":0,"targets_n":9,"title":"Rates, oil or an AI shock finally transmits to the index"}]'::jsonb, 'valid - Phase 3 held and narrowed: breadth through 50% to 49.50%, the Dow''s third straight losing week, CNN F&G 29, only the Nasdaq up, while every contraction condition moved away (VIX 14.81, MOVE down, HY flat, IG tighter)', 'valid - Phase 1 held; BTC defended the $74K falsifier by under $1,000 at $74,945 then cleared $80K, but the ETF week finished at +$6.2M and ETH''s four-week inflow streak snapped at −$140.6M', 'The mechanism was right and the market map split in two: every macro, rates, credit and oil band landed in S1 while every vol, crypto and metals band landed in S2, which is R5 recurring on the volatility-and-crypto axis. Underneath it, BTC was capped at $79K because the Fed was hiking - pricing the asset off the rates channel when the SEC''s agency track was the driver. Oil was mis-channelled the same way in W35, so this is now R12.', 7, 11, 0.105, false, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-21T00:00:00Z')
